.TH scan_html 3 "Version 1.0" "December 2023" "lib/textcode"
.SH NAME
scan_html, scan_html_tagarg \- Scan and decode HTML content
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/textcode.h>
.sp
.BI "size_t scan_html(const char* src, char* dest, size_t* destlen)"
.sp
.BI "size_t scan_html_tagarg(const char* src, char* dest, size_t* destlen)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The functions .BR scan_html () and .BR scan_html_tagarg () scan and decode HTML content. The functions take the following parameters:
.sp
1. A pointer to the source HTML string.
2. A pointer to the destination buffer.
3. A pointer to the size of the destination buffer.
.sp
The functions return the number of bytes processed from the source string.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of bytes processed from the source string.
.SH EXAMPLES
No examples are provided for these functions.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B fmt
